/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (In Sri Lanka, when the price of a crops goes up, a few farmers start growing it to make more money. Seeing this, many other farmers also started growing the same crop. When it's ready to harvest, there is too much of that crop in the market. This causes the prices to drop a lot, and farmers can't make enough money to cover their individual costs that it takes to make them. This cycle of high and low prices creates problems for farmers and the market.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [2]
